\textbf{Example (Q21-style):} In the circuit below, find the voltage across the 3-$\Omega$ resistor.

\bigskip
\textbf{Solution}

In the standard arrangement of this type of question, the 1-$\Omega$ and 3-$\Omega$ resistors are in parallel across a 6-V battery.

Since they are in parallel, the voltage across each is the same as the battery voltage:
$$V_3 = \boxed{6 \text{ V}}$$

\bigskip
\textbf{Water analogy:} The water pressure is the same across both parallel pipes. Both see the full pump pressure of 6 units.
\end{exercise}

